1
00:00:04,171 --> 00:00:05,589
- Go. Get the door.
- Here we are.

2
00:00:05,672 --> 00:00:06,798
Go. Push.

3
00:00:06,882 --> 00:00:08,383
- Oh, God.
- Push.

4
00:00:08,467 --> 00:00:10,111
No, no, no. Turn it
around. Really shove it.

5
00:00:10,135 --> 00:00:11,855
You'll break it. Shove
it through. Break it!

6
00:00:11,887 --> 00:00:14,014
You shove it. Shove it back.

7
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:18,060
Here we go.

8
00:00:18,519 --> 00:00:20,979
Don't break the
branches, Dwight.

9
00:00:21,647 --> 00:00:22,981
All right.

10
00:00:23,524 --> 00:00:26,568
I got a splinter. Well, suck
it up. We all have problems.

11
00:00:26,652 --> 00:00:29,279
Hey, everybody.
Look what we have.

12
00:00:32,032 --> 00:00:33,367
Nice, huh?

13
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:34,660
I've got it leveraged.

14
00:00:34,743 --> 00:00:36,137
- Push. Straight up.
- On three. Ready?

15
00:00:36,161 --> 00:00:38,580
- Big. One, two, three.
- One, two, three.

16
00:00:41,917 --> 00:00:43,544
Merry Christmas.

17
00:01:20,998 --> 00:01:22,541
Did it work?

18
00:01:22,624 --> 00:01:24,626
Well, sort of.

19
00:01:25,836 --> 00:01:27,963
Why did you get it so big?

20
00:01:28,046 --> 00:01:32,384
A, that's what she said, and,
B, I wanted it to be impressive.

21
00:01:32,467 --> 00:01:35,429
The biggest day of the year
deserves the biggest tree of the year.

22
00:01:35,512 --> 00:01:37,764
But what are we gonna
do with this hacked-off part?

23
00:01:37,848 --> 00:01:40,851
Well, that is a perfectly
good mini-tree, Kevin,

24
00:01:40,934 --> 00:01:43,645
and we are going
to sell that to charity.

25
00:01:43,729 --> 00:01:46,231
That's what
Christmas is all about.

26
00:01:54,364 --> 00:01:58,076
So this year, for the first time
ever, I got Pam in Secret Santa,

27
00:01:58,160 --> 00:01:59,995
and I got her this teapot,

28
00:02:00,078 --> 00:02:03,081
which I know she really wants,
so she can make tea at her desk.

29
00:02:03,165 --> 00:02:06,376
But I'm also gonna stuff
it with some inside jokes.

30
00:02:06,460 --> 00:02:09,713
Like, this is my high
school yearbook photo.

31
00:02:09,796 --> 00:02:13,258
She saw it at the party,
and it really makes her laugh.

32
00:02:13,592 --> 00:02:15,093
Not sure why.

33
00:02:15,844 --> 00:02:17,179
What else?

34
00:02:17,638 --> 00:02:19,640
This is a hot sauce packet.

35
00:02:19,723 --> 00:02:22,434
She put this on a hot
dog a couple years ago

36
00:02:22,517 --> 00:02:25,062
because she thought
it was ketchup.

37
00:02:25,562 --> 00:02:28,732
And it was really funny,
so I kept the other two.

38
00:02:29,524 --> 00:02:33,111
This would take a little too
long to explain, so I won't.

39
00:02:33,195 --> 00:02:34,988
And this is the card.

40
00:02:36,198 --> 00:02:39,826
Because Christmas is the
time to tell people how you feel.

41
00:02:42,579 --> 00:02:44,373
Is there anything we're missing?

42
00:02:44,456 --> 00:02:45,707
Phyllis, you got the lights?

43
00:02:45,791 --> 00:02:47,709
Yes, I got those
cute little ones.

44
00:02:49,294 --> 00:02:51,213
Do you think I should
have gotten the big ones?

45
00:02:51,296 --> 00:02:52,631
We'll see.

46
00:02:52,964 --> 00:02:55,967
<i>Angela drafted me into the
party planning committee.</i>

47
00:02:56,051 --> 00:03:00,305
Her memo said that we need to
prepare for every possible disaster,

48
00:03:01,682 --> 00:03:04,601
which to me seems excessive.

49
00:03:05,644 --> 00:03:10,065
Merry Christmas!
Ho, ho, ho, pimp.

50
00:03:10,857 --> 00:03:13,193
I'm kidding. What do
we got? What do we got?

51
00:03:13,276 --> 00:03:15,028
How many plates
are we getting? Fifty.

52
00:03:15,112 --> 00:03:17,781
Double it. Double everything.
Double ice cream. Double napkins.

53
00:03:17,864 --> 00:03:19,658
Double it. On me.

54
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:23,412
<i>It was a tough year. I had
to fire somebody this year.</i>

55
00:03:23,495 --> 00:03:25,622
This party has to really rock.

56
00:03:25,706 --> 00:03:29,418
Check it out. Christmas
bonus, 3,000 Gs.

57
00:03:29,501 --> 00:03:32,504
I got this for helping
save the company money.

58
00:03:33,004 --> 00:03:36,550
So I guess some good came
out of firing Devon after all.

59
00:03:36,758 --> 00:03:38,844
Maybe I should call
him and tell him that.

60
00:03:38,927 --> 00:03:43,515
I want people to cut loose. I
want people making out in closets.

61
00:03:44,516 --> 00:03:48,812
I want people hanging from the
ceilings, lamp shades on the heads.

62
00:03:48,895 --> 00:03:51,815
I want it to be a
Playboy Mansion party.

63
00:03:51,898 --> 00:03:56,111
And also, I want you to know and spread the
word that I will have my digital camera.

64
00:03:56,194 --> 00:03:58,780
And I'll be taking
pictures all along the way.

65
00:03:58,864 --> 00:04:01,158
And the best and
craziest thing that happens

66
00:04:01,241 --> 00:04:04,035
will be on the cover of
the newsletter. Incentive.

67
00:04:04,119 --> 00:04:06,371
You do realize that we
can't serve liquor at the party.

68
00:04:06,455 --> 00:04:08,331
Yeah. I know. Damn it.

69
00:04:08,498 --> 00:04:12,335
Stupid corporate wet blankets.
Like booze ever killed anybody.

70
00:04:13,462 --> 00:04:15,088
One. Two. Three.

71
00:04:16,965 --> 00:04:19,342
You guys should
use a hand truck.

72
00:04:19,426 --> 00:04:22,095
Do we have one? No.

73
00:04:25,766 --> 00:04:27,559
Will you help me?

74
00:04:28,310 --> 00:04:31,271
No! No way. It...
No. Come on, Mike.

75
00:04:31,354 --> 00:04:33,207
Let me borrow the hat
for just a couple of hours.

76
00:04:33,231 --> 00:04:34,566
You wanna be Santa? Yeah.

77
00:04:34,649 --> 00:04:35,984
Have you ever seen Santa?

78
00:04:36,067 --> 00:04:37,527
Yeah, I've seen Santa. Okay.

79
00:04:37,611 --> 00:04:40,530
Who cares? Well, I'm
sorry. It just doesn't work.

80
00:04:40,614 --> 00:04:43,200
Michael, I would
like to be the elf.

81
00:04:44,159 --> 00:04:46,995
That makes sense because
he has elfish features.

82
00:04:48,955 --> 00:04:50,248
<i>Okay, everyone. Listen up.</i>

83
00:04:51,041 --> 00:04:54,377
It is time to get your
presents, wrap them

84
00:04:54,461 --> 00:04:58,423
and place them
under the tree, like so.

85
00:04:59,674 --> 00:05:02,803
If you do not get your present
wrapped and under the tree

86
00:05:02,886 --> 00:05:05,138
within the next five minutes,

87
00:05:05,222 --> 00:05:08,350
you will be disqualified
from Secret Santa. All right?

88
00:05:08,433 --> 00:05:10,644
No exceptions except Michael.

89
00:05:11,186 --> 00:05:12,687
I got Angela.

90
00:05:13,146 --> 00:05:17,651
She is into these posters
of babies dressed as adults.

91
00:05:17,734 --> 00:05:19,694
<i>I got her one of those.</i>

92
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:22,739
I felt kind of
weird buying that.

93
00:05:23,198 --> 00:05:26,618
I got Creed. And to tell you the truth,
I don't know anything about Creed.

94
00:05:26,701 --> 00:05:29,663
I know his name's Creed. I
know he works right over there.

95
00:05:29,746 --> 00:05:31,873
I think he's Irish and I...

96
00:05:32,290 --> 00:05:35,335
I got him this
shamrock keychain.

97
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:39,172
I got myself for Secret Santa.

98
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:42,843
I was supposed to tell
somebody, but I didn't.

99
00:05:44,636 --> 00:05:46,721
You get something
good this year?

100
00:05:47,222 --> 00:05:50,600
I think I did a pretty good
job. Yeah? Who did you have?

101
00:05:50,684 --> 00:05:52,727
Well, I can't tell you,
'cause it's a secret.

102
00:05:52,811 --> 00:05:54,651
I think I got something
pretty nice for my guy.

103
00:05:54,688 --> 00:05:57,732
Yeah? I spent a lot of
dough. Lot of dough. Wow.

104
00:05:57,816 --> 00:06:00,068
Well, there's a $20
limit, right? So... Yeah.

105
00:06:00,151 --> 00:06:03,321
I wanted this party to be really special
so I sort of went above and beyond.

106
00:06:03,405 --> 00:06:05,508
That's great. Well, don't tell
me who it is, 'cause I can...

107
00:06:05,532 --> 00:06:09,494
It was Ryan. Yeah. I have Ryan.

108
00:06:09,578 --> 00:06:13,832
Gather round. Secret Santa,
let's go. Let's go. Come on.

109
00:06:14,082 --> 00:06:17,168
Stanley, no. I'm gonna handle
the cord. Okay, safety reasons.

110
00:06:17,252 --> 00:06:18,712
I know how to plug something in.

111
00:06:18,795 --> 00:06:20,171
I want to do it.

112
00:06:20,255 --> 00:06:24,885
All right, let's count it down,
like Rockefeller Center.

113
00:06:24,968 --> 00:06:26,136
Ready?

114
00:06:26,678 --> 00:06:29,848
- Three, two, one.
- Three, two, one.

115
00:06:32,976 --> 00:06:34,436
Not great.

116
00:06:34,519 --> 00:06:36,187
I'm sorry, everybody.

117
00:06:37,147 --> 00:06:38,857
I think the tree looks nice.

118
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:40,901
Hey, I could get some
flares from my car.

119
00:06:40,984 --> 00:06:44,571
No. No. Shake it off, everybody.
Just, let's do Secret Santa.

120
00:06:44,779 --> 00:06:48,491
Presents are the best way to
show someone how much you care.

121
00:06:49,242 --> 00:06:52,245
It is like this tangible thing
that you can point to and say,

122
00:06:52,329 --> 00:06:55,624
"Hey, man, I love you
this many dollars' worth."

123
00:06:56,124 --> 00:06:57,918
First present, Oscar.

124
00:07:02,130 --> 00:07:03,298
Shower radio. Neat.

125
00:07:03,381 --> 00:07:04,591
Oh, good, that was from me.

126
00:07:04,674 --> 00:07:06,527
Thanks, Kelly. You know
I was gonna get one of...

127
00:07:06,551 --> 00:07:09,387
Okay. Okay. That's enough.
Let's keep it moving on.

128
00:07:09,471 --> 00:07:11,640
Jim. Oh, cool.

129
00:07:15,936 --> 00:07:16,937
That's from me.

130
00:07:17,020 --> 00:07:18,063
Great.

131
00:07:19,189 --> 00:07:20,607
Where did you get it?

132
00:07:20,690 --> 00:07:22,692
I don't know. It
was so long ago.

133
00:07:22,817 --> 00:07:25,111
He obviously forgot
to get me something,

134
00:07:25,195 --> 00:07:28,406
and then he went into his closet
and dug out this little number

135
00:07:28,490 --> 00:07:29,950
and then threw it in a bag.

136
00:07:30,075 --> 00:07:31,952
Yep. That's exactly
what happened.

137
00:07:32,035 --> 00:07:33,203
Pam.

138
00:07:41,127 --> 00:07:42,671
Oh, my God!

139
00:07:44,089 --> 00:07:47,133
Thank you very much,
Santa, whoever you are.

140
00:07:47,717 --> 00:07:49,970
It's awesome. There's
a little more to it.

141
00:07:50,053 --> 00:07:51,429
All right. Next.

142
00:07:51,513 --> 00:07:53,223
Ryan. No. Don't.

143
00:07:58,103 --> 00:08:00,271
Whoa, a video iPod.

144
00:08:00,355 --> 00:08:02,565
Whoa. Wow. Jeez.

145
00:08:03,024 --> 00:08:06,486
Somebody really got carried
away with the spirit of Christmas.

146
00:08:06,569 --> 00:08:08,738
That was me. I got
carried away with the spirit.

147
00:08:08,822 --> 00:08:11,449
Wasn't there a
$20 limit on the gift?

148
00:08:12,283 --> 00:08:13,952
This is 400 bucks.

149
00:08:14,077 --> 00:08:15,453
You don't know that.

150
00:08:15,537 --> 00:08:16,764
Yeah, you left the price tag on.

151
00:08:16,788 --> 00:08:17,789
I did? Yeah.

152
00:08:17,872 --> 00:08:19,541
What? Oh, shoot. Wow.

153
00:08:19,624 --> 00:08:22,502
Okay, well, who cares? It
doesn't matter what I spent.

154
00:08:22,585 --> 00:08:25,588
What matters is that
Christmas is fun, right?

155
00:08:27,132 --> 00:08:30,135
Michael. Oh, hey, for me.

156
00:08:31,011 --> 00:08:33,888
What is in here?

157
00:08:35,807 --> 00:08:37,267
Oh, come on.

158
00:08:37,350 --> 00:08:38,768
I knitted it for you.

159
00:08:39,602 --> 00:08:41,104
An oven mitt?

160
00:08:41,896 --> 00:08:43,023
Okay.

161
00:08:44,733 --> 00:08:46,276
<i>So Phyllis is basically saying,</i>

162
00:08:46,359 --> 00:08:48,919
<i>"Hey, Michael, I know you did
a lot to help the office this year"</i>

163
00:08:48,945 --> 00:08:52,490
"but I only care about you a
homemade oven mitt's worth."

164
00:08:52,574 --> 00:08:54,325
I gave Ryan an iPod.

165
00:08:57,912 --> 00:09:01,207
Should we just keep
opening up the presents?

166
00:09:01,291 --> 00:09:05,378
We don't do anything until
Michael gives us further instructions.

167
00:09:09,007 --> 00:09:10,175
I got it.

168
00:09:10,341 --> 00:09:12,510
We are going to turn

169
00:09:12,594 --> 00:09:15,847
Secret Santa into Yankee Swap.

170
00:09:16,056 --> 00:09:17,474
What is Yankee Swap?

171
00:09:17,557 --> 00:09:19,934
One person chooses a gift.

172
00:09:20,018 --> 00:09:24,939
The next person can either choose
a gift or steal that person's gift.

173
00:09:25,315 --> 00:09:28,902
If your gift gets stolen, then
you can steal someone else's gift

174
00:09:28,985 --> 00:09:30,361
or choose a new gift.

175
00:09:30,445 --> 00:09:32,197
I thought that was
called Nasty Christmas.

176
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:33,865
Yeah, we call it White Elephant.

177
00:09:33,948 --> 00:09:35,658
Well, I call it fun!

178
00:09:35,742 --> 00:09:36,951
Why are we doing this?

179
00:09:37,035 --> 00:09:38,953
Because it's better.
Because it's more special.

180
00:09:39,037 --> 00:09:40,497
It sounds mean. Shut it.

181
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:43,583
No, it's not... Okay,
just give it a shot.

182
00:09:43,875 --> 00:09:46,795
Michael should have asked
the party planning committee first.

183
00:09:46,878 --> 00:09:50,965
He's not supposed to just spring
things on us out of nowhere.

184
00:09:55,553 --> 00:09:59,140
Okay, Meredith is up
first. Here's the deal.

185
00:09:59,224 --> 00:10:01,017
You can either pick a new gift

186
00:10:01,101 --> 00:10:03,394
or you can steal
somebody else's gift

187
00:10:03,478 --> 00:10:05,688
that they've already
gotten, like the oven mitt.

188
00:10:06,064 --> 00:10:07,398
I'll take the teapot.

189
00:10:07,482 --> 00:10:09,234
Oh. Shouldn't we...

190
00:10:10,151 --> 00:10:12,862
I bought that specifically
for Pam. Yankee Swap!

191
00:10:12,946 --> 00:10:14,322
That's what makes it fun.

192
00:10:14,405 --> 00:10:17,242
Pam, you can steal the oven
mitt now. I'll take the iPod.

193
00:10:17,325 --> 00:10:19,577
And I have to give it to
her? I don't have a choice?

194
00:10:19,702 --> 00:10:21,871
Yes. Now, you can
steal the oven mitt,

195
00:10:21,955 --> 00:10:25,333
the old shirt or the shower
radio or pick a new gift.

196
00:10:36,928 --> 00:10:39,806
That was meant for
Kelly. Yeah, I figured.

197
00:10:44,811 --> 00:10:46,980
I think this is going great.

198
00:10:56,447 --> 00:10:57,615
Yikes.

199
00:10:57,907 --> 00:11:00,034
Well, it's for Angela, so...

200
00:11:03,079 --> 00:11:05,415
That's, like, the creepiest
thing that I've ever seen.

201
00:11:05,498 --> 00:11:07,167
Angela, you're up.

202
00:11:10,253 --> 00:11:12,046
I'll take the poster.

203
00:11:14,757 --> 00:11:16,676
Some people like these.

204
00:11:17,135 --> 00:11:19,137
I will steal the iPod.

205
00:11:19,971 --> 00:11:21,222
<i>Everyone wants the iPod.</i>

206
00:11:21,306 --> 00:11:24,934
It's a huge hit. It is almost
a Christmas miracle.

207
00:11:25,935 --> 00:11:30,857
Oh, well, Oscar, you little
gourmand, you have the next turn.

208
00:11:30,940 --> 00:11:35,195
I'll take the teapot. Damn it.

209
00:11:35,278 --> 00:11:37,906
Okay. Moving along,
Meredith, let's go.

210
00:11:38,531 --> 00:11:39,991
I really want the iPod.

211
00:11:41,201 --> 00:11:43,429
It's already been stolen this
round. Pick something else.

212
00:11:43,453 --> 00:11:46,581
I hope nobody takes this
baby, 'cause this is great.

213
00:11:46,664 --> 00:11:49,292
Wow, look at that
fine craftsmanship.

214
00:11:50,335 --> 00:11:53,630
Somebody really put a lot
of work into that. It's beautiful.

215
00:11:53,713 --> 00:11:55,715
I'll take the oven mitt.

216
00:11:57,467 --> 00:11:59,052
Sucker!

217
00:12:00,386 --> 00:12:04,015
See, I wanted somebody to take
it. Boom! Reverse psychology.

218
00:12:04,098 --> 00:12:06,726
Reverse psychology
is an awesome tool.

219
00:12:07,143 --> 00:12:08,978
I don't know if you
guys know about it,

220
00:12:09,062 --> 00:12:13,775
but basically you make someone
think the opposite of what you believe

221
00:12:14,025 --> 00:12:17,362
and that tricks them into
doing something stupid.

222
00:12:17,862 --> 00:12:19,113
Works like a charm.

223
00:12:25,954 --> 00:12:27,622
"In addition to these
paint ball pellets,"

224
00:12:27,705 --> 00:12:31,209
"your gift includes two paint
ball lessons with Dwight Shrute."

225
00:12:31,292 --> 00:12:33,586
You and me, Michael. Yes.

226
00:12:37,423 --> 00:12:41,678
Who wants to take paint ball lessons?
How is that better than an iPod?

227
00:12:41,761 --> 00:12:44,472
I never said it was
better than an iPod.

228
00:12:47,058 --> 00:12:50,395
Michael keeps bragging about
his iPod, but you know what?

229
00:12:50,478 --> 00:12:53,022
Two paint ball lessons with
someone as experienced as I am

230
00:12:53,106 --> 00:12:55,358
is worth easily, like, 2 grand.

231
00:12:55,858 --> 00:12:57,568
Take that, Saddam.

232
00:12:57,735 --> 00:12:59,279
Last gift, Kevin.

233
00:12:59,362 --> 00:13:00,989
I want the foot bath.

234
00:13:04,409 --> 00:13:06,160
<i>That's the thing
I bought myself.</i>

235
00:13:06,452 --> 00:13:08,663
I'm really psyched to use it.

236
00:13:11,124 --> 00:13:13,626
Maybe I should
have taken the iPod.

237
00:13:15,586 --> 00:13:17,213
Oh, shoot.

238
00:13:18,089 --> 00:13:20,800
Pam, steal something
or pick the final gift.

239
00:13:20,883 --> 00:13:23,177
- I want the iPod.
- Damn it.

240
00:13:23,261 --> 00:13:25,471
Sure you don't want the teapot?

241
00:13:25,555 --> 00:13:28,391
Well, I mean, it's
an iPod. But... Right.

242
00:13:28,474 --> 00:13:30,810
Sorry, I... No. No.
Definitely. It's...

243
00:13:30,893 --> 00:13:35,648
Okay, well, I guess I will
take that book of short stories.

244
00:13:36,024 --> 00:13:40,028
Yes! There you go. I
want the tea pot. <i>Gracias.</i>

245
00:13:41,321 --> 00:13:42,405
Got to be kidding me.

246
00:13:42,739 --> 00:13:46,993
Yankee Swap is
like Machiavelli meets

247
00:13:49,579 --> 00:13:50,663
Christmas.

248
00:13:52,498 --> 00:13:53,791
What is she so upset about?

249
00:13:53,875 --> 00:13:55,793
Maybe because you
hated her present so much.

250
00:13:55,877 --> 00:13:58,087
Come on! I think that
Yankee Swap was a big hit.

251
00:13:58,171 --> 00:13:59,589
I think it was a success,

252
00:13:59,672 --> 00:14:02,392
and I'm the one who ended up
with Dwight's stupid paint ball pellets.

253
00:14:02,467 --> 00:14:05,845
Yeah, but, Michael, the point is that
we all bought gifts for specific people.

254
00:14:05,928 --> 00:14:08,556
And you should have just bought
a $20 gift like everyone else.

255
00:14:08,639 --> 00:14:09,766
Well, I didn't.

256
00:14:09,849 --> 00:14:12,393
I got a big bonus
because I fired Devon,

257
00:14:12,477 --> 00:14:15,271
and I used the money to buy
something awesome. Sue me!

258
00:14:17,231 --> 00:14:19,025
You got a bonus check?

259
00:14:19,192 --> 00:14:20,443
How much?

260
00:14:20,943 --> 00:14:25,198
It wasn't... It wasn't
that much. It was $3,000.

261
00:14:25,531 --> 00:14:27,533
All right, I'm done now.

262
00:14:30,953 --> 00:14:32,121
<i>Unbelievable.</i>

263
00:14:32,205 --> 00:14:34,791
<i>I do the nicest thing that anyone
has ever done for these people,</i>

264
00:14:34,874 --> 00:14:36,000
<i>and they freak out.</i>

265
00:14:36,084 --> 00:14:39,670
Well, happy birthday, Jesus.
Sorry your party's so lame.

266
00:14:43,049 --> 00:14:45,009
It comes to $166.41.

267
00:14:45,093 --> 00:14:49,389
All right, now, you're the expert. Is
this enough to get 20 people plastered?

268
00:14:50,348 --> 00:14:52,433
Fifteen bottles of vodka?

269
00:14:53,059 --> 00:14:56,229
Yeah, that should do
it. Cool, cool. Box it up.

270
00:15:06,697 --> 00:15:09,492
I bought this teapot for Pam,
and I know she really wants it.

271
00:15:09,575 --> 00:15:11,411
So, can I trade you
for it? No trades.

272
00:15:11,494 --> 00:15:14,414
Come on. It's a shamrock
keychain. Good luck.

273
00:15:14,705 --> 00:15:18,292
"A real man makes his
own luck." Billy Zane, <i>Titanic.</i>

274
00:15:18,376 --> 00:15:21,671
Look it has sentimental value,
Dwight. Can I buy it from you?

275
00:15:21,754 --> 00:15:23,714
No. I want it. I'm
going to use it.

276
00:15:23,798 --> 00:15:25,425
You don't even drink tea. True.

277
00:15:25,508 --> 00:15:28,636
But I get sinus infections, and
sinus infections can be cured

278
00:15:28,719 --> 00:15:30,680
by making your tea from
green tea leaf stems...

279
00:15:30,763 --> 00:15:32,056
Okay. And pouring it directly

280
00:15:32,140 --> 00:15:33,683
into your nose, like so.

281
00:15:37,061 --> 00:15:40,523
To think that my gift to
Pam will be used for that,

282
00:15:41,441 --> 00:15:43,609
it's a little too
much to handle.

283
00:15:43,693 --> 00:15:44,861
This is awesome.

284
00:15:44,944 --> 00:15:47,488
I know. It's totally gonna
change the way I work out.

285
00:15:47,572 --> 00:15:51,117
Yeah, I was gonna get you one of
these for Christmas, now I don't have to.

286
00:15:51,200 --> 00:15:52,386
I'm gonna save a ton of money.

287
00:15:52,410 --> 00:15:53,762
So what are you
gonna get me instead?

288
00:15:53,786 --> 00:15:56,414
I don't know. Probably,
like, a sweater or something.

289
00:15:59,709 --> 00:16:00,710
Uh-oh.

290
00:16:00,835 --> 00:16:04,005
Looks like Santa
was a little naughty.

291
00:16:05,506 --> 00:16:06,924
What is that?

292
00:16:07,008 --> 00:16:11,012
This is Christmas
spirit, as in spirits, booze.

293
00:16:11,345 --> 00:16:12,763
We can drink?

294
00:16:12,847 --> 00:16:14,932
We're really not
supposed to serve alcohol.

295
00:16:15,016 --> 00:16:18,269
Zip it, Toby! Just... I
mean, it's a party. Come on.

296
00:16:18,352 --> 00:16:22,398
If I can't throw a good party for my
employees, then I am a terrible boss.

297
00:16:23,816 --> 00:16:25,276
Who wants a drink? Me. Please.

298
00:16:25,359 --> 00:16:26,903
Go! Here we go!

299
00:16:28,279 --> 00:16:30,281
<i>The deal is that
this is my last hurrah,</i>

300
00:16:30,364 --> 00:16:32,783
'cause I made a
New Year's resolution

301
00:16:32,867 --> 00:16:36,162
that I'm not gonna drink
anymore during the week.

302
00:16:36,579 --> 00:16:38,164
- Hi, guys.
- Hey.

303
00:16:38,247 --> 00:16:40,833
Does everyone know
my boyfriend, Bob Vance?

304
00:16:40,917 --> 00:16:43,961
Kevin Malone. Bob
Vance, Vance Refrigeration.

305
00:16:44,045 --> 00:16:46,923
Stanley Hudson. Bob
Vance, Vance Refrigeration.

306
00:16:47,006 --> 00:16:49,926
Ryan Howard. Bob
Vance, Vance Refrigeration.

307
00:16:51,594 --> 00:16:53,846
What line of work you in, Bob?

308
00:16:54,347 --> 00:16:57,475
I think after I lost Culpepper
and T.O. it was over, man.

309
00:16:57,558 --> 00:16:59,310
Oh, yeah, I need McMahon,

310
00:16:59,393 --> 00:17:01,896
Deion Branch to have big
games, or else I'm done.

311
00:17:01,979 --> 00:17:03,105
It's possible.

312
00:17:03,189 --> 00:17:05,107
I can't believe you traded
Shaun Alexander, man.

313
00:17:05,191 --> 00:17:06,400
I had to, I needed defense.

314
00:17:06,484 --> 00:17:07,860
Come on! Shaun Alexander?

315
00:17:07,944 --> 00:17:10,196
He's the best back in the league.
- It's defense.

316
00:17:10,279 --> 00:17:12,949
Oh, no. That's not worth it.
- It is worth it.

317
00:17:13,032 --> 00:17:15,159
Never. DARRYL: Are
you kidding? You wait.

318
00:17:15,243 --> 00:17:19,455
Anybody making out in
here? Not yet. Give it time.

319
00:17:19,830 --> 00:17:21,832
Oh, hey, Ebenezer, boink.

320
00:17:21,916 --> 00:17:23,709
Okay, how's it going in here?

321
00:17:23,793 --> 00:17:26,188
We're running low on cups. Do you
want me to just run out and get some?

322
00:17:26,212 --> 00:17:27,397
Yeah, there should
be some... No, no, no.

323
00:17:27,421 --> 00:17:29,006
We'll find some.
Don't leave the party.

324
00:17:29,090 --> 00:17:31,509
One, two, three!

325
00:17:36,556 --> 00:17:38,849
Kudos to Ryan, king
of the party committee.

326
00:17:38,933 --> 00:17:40,101
- Oh, no.
- Yeah. Yeah. Yeah.

327
00:17:40,184 --> 00:17:41,519
I really did not do anything.

328
00:17:41,602 --> 00:17:43,437
Oh, no, no. No false
modesty, my friend.

329
00:17:48,192 --> 00:17:50,820
You know, you don't have
to answer calls during a party.

330
00:17:50,903 --> 00:17:52,405
Just thought you should know.

331
00:17:52,488 --> 00:17:55,366
No, I was just checking
out my present.

332
00:17:57,910 --> 00:18:00,162
But... I traded with Dwight.

333
00:18:01,706 --> 00:18:03,457
Just, I figured, you know,

334
00:18:03,541 --> 00:18:06,002
you went to a lot of
trouble and it means a lot.

335
00:18:07,503 --> 00:18:10,381
And also, Roy got me an iPod

336
00:18:11,299 --> 00:18:13,759
or was going to
get me an iPod, so...

337
00:18:14,135 --> 00:18:15,761
Well, either way.

338
00:18:16,887 --> 00:18:20,308
This is an amazing gift
because it comes with bonus gifts.

339
00:18:21,392 --> 00:18:22,768
Look inside.

340
00:18:27,690 --> 00:18:32,111
Oh, my God! The
yearbook picture.

341
00:18:32,320 --> 00:18:34,947
Yeah, I think I made
the right choice.

342
00:18:36,073 --> 00:18:39,285
Oh, my God! It's incredible.

343
00:18:39,368 --> 00:18:40,578
Is this the bottle timer?

344
00:18:40,661 --> 00:18:43,021
I didn't think you were gonna
get that one. I really didn't.

345
00:18:44,915 --> 00:18:46,667
This is so awesome.

346
00:18:46,834 --> 00:18:50,421
Not bad. And if it couldn't go to Ryan,
you are the guy I'd want it to go to.

347
00:18:50,504 --> 00:18:51,714
Thank you. You're welcome.

348
00:18:51,797 --> 00:18:54,133
Merry Christmas,
asswipe. No way.

349
00:18:54,216 --> 00:18:57,470
Oh, you're kidding me. Packer!

350
00:18:57,970 --> 00:19:01,265
Yes! Todd Packer,
ladies and gentlemen.

351
00:19:01,432 --> 00:19:04,018
What's up, my
nerds? Check it out!

352
00:19:04,101 --> 00:19:08,522
Oh, no, no. Oh, look at
that. Icing on the cake.

353
00:19:09,065 --> 00:19:11,734
Pacman need a drinky.
Oh, let's fix you up.

354
00:19:11,817 --> 00:19:14,737
Who wants to fix up... Toby?
Toby's gonna fix you up.

355
00:19:15,154 --> 00:19:16,280
Yeah.

356
00:19:21,118 --> 00:19:23,537
Darryl. There you go.

357
00:19:23,621 --> 00:19:25,247
You earned it.
That's okay, Mike.

358
00:19:25,331 --> 00:19:28,459
No, no, no, no. I really,
really want you to have it.

359
00:19:28,542 --> 00:19:30,419
All right. Thanks, man.

360
00:19:30,503 --> 00:19:32,296
Hey, Merry Christmas.

361
00:19:34,590 --> 00:19:37,218
Whose butt is that? Mine.

362
00:19:37,301 --> 00:19:39,553
Oh, how did I not guess that?

363
00:19:39,637 --> 00:19:43,683
Lampshade on
head! It's happening!

364
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:45,768
Oh, no.

365
00:19:54,276 --> 00:19:56,570
Hey. Oh, hello there.

366
00:19:59,323 --> 00:20:02,284
But what are you
doing? I don't know.

367
00:20:02,660 --> 00:20:05,871
You shouldn't do things like that.
The man is supposed to do that.

368
00:20:19,301 --> 00:20:21,220
- Thanks for the party, Michael.
- Yeah.

369
00:20:21,303 --> 00:20:23,514
Oh, hey... Listen up. We're
going to Poor Richard's.

370
00:20:23,597 --> 00:20:24,724
Who's in? I'm in.

371
00:20:24,807 --> 00:20:25,933
Yes.

372
00:20:26,016 --> 00:20:28,185
Michael? Poor Richard's?

373
00:20:29,395 --> 00:20:30,938
Yeah. That sounds good.

374
00:20:31,021 --> 00:20:32,857
Christmas is awesome.

375
00:20:33,482 --> 00:20:37,236
First of all, you get to spend
time with people you love.

376
00:20:37,319 --> 00:20:40,990
<i>Secondly, you can get drunk
and no one can say anything.</i>

377
00:20:41,073 --> 00:20:44,785
<i>Third, you give presents. What's
better than giving presents?</i>

378
00:20:44,869 --> 00:20:48,831
<i>And fourth, getting presents. So,
four things. Not bad for one day.</i>

379
00:20:48,914 --> 00:20:52,042
It's really the greatest
day of all time.

380
00:20:54,712 --> 00:20:55,880
Hey, Meredith.

381
00:20:55,963 --> 00:20:58,007
Heading over to
Poor Richard's? Yep.

382
00:20:58,090 --> 00:21:01,343
Cool, cool, cool.
Do you need a ride?

383
00:21:11,395 --> 00:21:13,439
All right, let's head out.

384
00:21:14,190 --> 00:21:17,401
Sounds good. Do
you have a coat? Yeah.

385
00:21:17,485 --> 00:21:18,778
Okay!

